/* Modern theme for the system menu -- uses base.rcss's shared forged-dialog shell (also used by
   Login), with the metal .modern-header-rail/.modern-joint header variant instead of Login's
   crimson hero-banner (see this file's own sys_menu.rml note). #panel keeps base.rcss's shared
   .modern-frame for its material fill/gradient (no -crimson variant -- crimson belongs to a
   hero-banner's own plate, this dialog has none), with background/border/box-shadow overridden
   here to the same neutral forged-window surface Login's own #panel uses (mirrored rather than
   shared via .modern-frame itself, so this change doesn't silently affect .modern-frame's other
   consumers -- msg_win/my_quest_info/remember_password_prompt/my_inventory_bg -- which haven't
   been revisited yet). No hero-banner glow here -- that's Login's own header style, not this
   dialog's. Header carries a title (base.rcss's .modern-header-text/-title, bound to
   SysMenuRmlModel's systemMenuLabel -- I18N::Game::SystemMenu). Buttons rely entirely on
   base.rcss's shared .btn -- no per-window color override needed or present.

   #panel is not C++-positioned/sized -- centered via base.rcss's .center-both utility class
   (applied in sys_menu.rml). width (213dp) is unchanged (CWinEx's own real sprite-width
   geometry); height grew by 31dp (187->218, compact 155->186) to make room for the real 38dp-tall
   metal header rail (top:7dp) replacing the old 10dp decorative cap strip -- the previous height
   was sized for that thin strip, not a real banner. Button positions absorb this the same way
   they already absorb the .compact height difference: exit-game/select-server anchor from the
   top and shifted down by the same 31dp the header grew by (33->64, 67->98, preserving the
   original 4dp gap between them and the 4dp/6dp gaps down to option below in both compact and
   non-compact mode); option/close anchor from the bottom and need no change at all, since the
   growth happened entirely at the top.

   #btn_option/#btn_close's `bottom` values are the old C++'s "distance from panel bottom to the
   button's TOP" (86/52) minus the button's own 30dp height, not those numbers directly -- CSS
   `bottom` measures to the button's BOTTOM edge, not its top. Using 86/52 as-is would put every
   bottom-anchored button 30dp higher than intended, overlapping #btn_select_server above it. */
#panel {
	width: 213dp;
	height: 218dp;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 12dp;
	color: token(text-primary);
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;
	background-color: #080a08;
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, #11130f 0%, #080a08 100%);
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: token(border-frame);
	box-shadow:
		0 11dp 30dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 158),
		0 2dp 5dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 217),
		inset 0 0 0 1dp #090a08,
		inset 0 0 0 3dp rgba(120, 115, 90, 190);
}
#panel.compact {
	height: 186dp;
}

#btn_exit_game    { left: 52dp; top: 64dp; }
#btn_select_server{ left: 52dp; top: 98dp; }
#btn_option       { left: 52dp; bottom: 56dp; }
#btn_close        { left: 52dp; bottom: 22dp; }
